WEBVTT

NOTE Captions for t2-01-safe-conversation.mp3 — machine-transcribed on-device from the existing audio (SR-472). Not proofread.
NOTE Cues with ids phase-recognise/-regulate/-release/-rise mark where each step begins; js/saferise-poster.js reads them.

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:08.680
There is a conversation you haven't had yet in reality, but your mind has
already run this crypt a 11 times.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:12.330
Playing both parts to ensure you know exactly how it ends.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:17.780
This process focuses entirely on the state you are in before you speak a
single word.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:32.007
It leaves the actual conversation up to you. What you say, how you say it, or
whether you choose to have it at all. The body braces for impact first, while

00:00:32.007 --> 00:00:36.560
the grounded presence that actually knows how to connect takes time to arrive.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:46.990
Most of your exhaustion is born in the friction between those two states.

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:54.960
Holding your breath before you cross the river does not make the water any
shallower. You still have to step in and you will do it better breathing.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.290
Let's move through the next four distinct phases.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:00:59.790
Step by step

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:01.840
Starting with Recognise

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:20.550
Fine where this anticipation has settled in your body. Usually it sits as a
tight band across the top of the chest, a subtle closing of the throat.

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:28.330
A hollowness behind the ribs.

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:34.800
Or hands that desperately want something to grip. Give this physical state a
single word, agitated.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:42.610
Stay with it for a moment. Don't move past it yet. Notice exactly what that
word leaves out. It leaves out the other person's humanity.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:46.850
What they will actually say, how they will receive it, and what happens next.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:52.860
The event hasn't occurred yet your nervous system is reacting as if you have
already survived the collision.

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:55.810
Now go one layer deeper into the shadows

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:06.190
Beneath the rehearsed words lies a deeper concern about what a bad outcome
will mean for you.

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:08.610
Stay there for one full breath.

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:17.460
Don't explain it. Just let it be visible. One layer further down.

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:24.430
Look closely at the primary driver underneath

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:28.580
Losing control of the narrative being left totally isolated

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:33.840
Being exposed as the villain of the story or running out of time to fix a bond
that matters.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:36.760
Notice which one landed closest.

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:39.740
Sink into that core vulnerability.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:53.857
Leave it right where it is. Nothing needs to be solved here. Ready to
regulate? To do this, we'll soften the physical armor. Starting in the exact

00:02:53.857 --> 00:02:55.170
places you just found.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:02.280
Draw a slow breath in for four counts

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.300
And release it for six counts.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:18.320
Keep the exhale longer than the inhale every single time. 10 seconds cycle.
That is the page your heart rhythm settles into when you stop fighting it.

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:26.578
8. Pay specific attention to your throat. The ego guards the throat when it
feels threatened, altering the pitch and tone of your voice before you even

00:03:26.578 --> 00:03:27.040
speak. 8.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:31.720
Let your jaw on the hinge slightly, let your tongue drop away from the roof of
your mouth.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:38.840
Now that tight bend across the chest

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:42.960
Let your shoulders come down away from your ears and let the band go slack.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:45.440
Nothing is bracing against anything yet.

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:46.410
And your hands.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:54.660
If they are gripping or looking for something, the grip opened them.

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:04.810
Spread the fingers wide, hold for a moment.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.850
Then let them for completely loose.

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:08.380
On your next out breath

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.260
Feel it vibrate in the throat and the

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:19.280
The exact place that was closing.

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:29.920
That vibration is doing two things at once.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:33.120
It is opening the throat you're about to speak with.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:45.570
And it is lengthening your exhale without you having to count. Hum once more,
a little longer, and let it fade out.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:47.290
rather than stopping it.

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:59.200
Now bring your attention directly into the center of your chest

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:02.630
If resting a hand there helps anchor you, do it.

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:10.950
Keep the breath moving through that point in for four out for six.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:21.360
And as you breathe there, bring to mind one thing you genuinely value about
this person or about what you have built with them, not a strategy.

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:31.101
Something true. Hold it steady at the chest, while the breath passes through.
A steady rhythm alone will settle you. A steady rhythm with warmth behind it

00:05:31.101 --> 00:05:33.760
is what changes how you walk into the room.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:40.860
Thoughts of the argument will crash in. Let them arrive without pushing them
away, following the logic or letting them finish their sentences.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:42.780
It's an arising thought.

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:52.030
It's just a phantom echo, it is not a command to brace yourself. If you notice
yourself trying hard to calm down, ease off. Watching requires no effort.

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:55.550
Striving means your ego has just found a new way to fight.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:08.370
Shadow stretch across a floor, but the floor does not become the dark.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.650
There are two separate things occurring right now.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:20.450
There is your physical state

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:25.390
Which arrive because this relationship matters and you are about to step into
the unknown.

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:29.040
And then there is the drafting, running the dialogue in advance.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:32.350
predicting the defense and sharpening your counterpoints.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:34.390
Third stage release.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:44.220
The ego calls this drafting preparation. But past the second run through, it
ceases to be preparation and becomes an endless argument with a ghost.

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:46.840
Notice how the draft always end.

00:06:52.340 --> 00:07:00.947
You always have the flawless and penetrable final line. That is because the
part of you writing this script, it is designed to protect you from

00:07:00.947 --> 00:07:01.790
vulnerability.

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:05.800
So it guarantees you win, but every time you run that script,

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:09.420
Your nervous system experiences the fight all over again.

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:21.320
You have already had this conversation 11 times and none of them counted.

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:28.660
Let the physical stage remain. It is here because you care, but put down the
script. Ask yourself gently.

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:41.980
What was this mental rehearsal built to protect?

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:52.870
Scripting a conversation is what we do when speaking the truth has causes
dearly in the past.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:02.170
It is a protective shield earned through old wounds.

00:08:02.630 --> 00:08:04.050
Sit with that for a moment

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:08.240
Something in you learned that going in on armored was dangerous.

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:10.890
That was not foolishness, it was experience.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:13.170
You don't need to dissect it today.

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:21.680
Keep the inquiry for later and notice the hearted truth underneath.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:30.650
A part of you does not want to drop descript.

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:38.736
Because the script is the only thing guaranteeing you won't be caught off
guard. Name that rather than arguing with it. A rehearse defense guarantees

00:08:38.736 --> 00:08:40.100
you will not be surprised.

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:48.190
But it also guarantees you will not actually connect. You cannot armor
yourself and reach someone with the same gesture. Put the underlying fear of

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:51.510
rejection where your breath is and let it go out with the hum.

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:03.050
None of this gets settled in the rehearsal. Finally, we rise.

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:06.060
Finally, we step into open presence.

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:13.000
Visualize yourself from across the room.

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:21.860
Moments away from saying something difficult.

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:30.510
You have something true to say and you are allowed to say it imperfectly.

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:42.020
Now picture the version of yourself you want to embody in that room

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:47.440
Same stakes

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:49.010
Same racing heart.

00:09:54.860 --> 00:10:02.900
But you are the one deciding where your attention anchors, not on predicting
their reaction, but on the integrity of your own first sentence.

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:05.830
Where are you sitting? What are your hands doing?

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:09.110
What are the actual unshielded words you open with?

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:22.716
Step directly into that grounded reality. The nerves are still present, but
your attention belongs to the present moment. Not the worst case scenario.

00:10:22.716 --> 00:10:27.870
Pick the exact sentence you will use to open the door. Afterwards, write down
what shifted.

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:35.980
Take one last slow breath, in for four and out for six.

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:38.920
Let this one carry the home if you can.

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:45.040
Feel the solid floor supporting you, roll your shoulders slowly, letting the
tension in your neck loosen.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:54.770
Stretch your arms out and open your eyes when you are ready.

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:05.220
Return to this anchor whenever you need to trade your armor

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:06.680
For authentic connection.

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:17.340
The water is the same depth either way.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:23.400
Go in breathing.
